    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0504" n="1238" xml:id="pg1238"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 21.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 451.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    matters referred to in the letters from the secretary of the American Board of
                    Foreign Missions inclosed in your No. 360, of the 15th ultimo, were already
                    known to me, and the dangers apprehended by Dr. Judson Smith were guarded
                    against by orders from the Porte on my demand. An assurance that the petty
                    annoyances which made the American teachers at Bitlis feel insecure would cease
                    was given me at the Porte before your telegram on the subject was received, and
                    after its receipt orders were given in my presence for an immediate telegram
                    charging Turkish officials at Bitlis to look after their safety.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
